cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or cite Civilodynamics, please cite the canonical corpus as below."
title: "Civilodynamics: Canonical Corpus"
abstract: >-
  Civilodynamics is the quantitative science of how civilizations maintain
  coherence, accumulate stress, approach phase transitions, and reorganize,
  with particular attention to the role of information architecture. The
  canonical corpus comprises a Foundational Charter, mathematical and
  methodological foundations, poliform theory, a measurement program and data
  architecture, a flagship U.S. case study, a retrodiction casebook, a lexicon
  and ontology, and a living program map, together with building-phase
  instrument documents. The framework is, at this stage, a falsifiable
  skeleton; reported quantities are illustrative estimates pending computation.
type: dataset
